{
  "_comment": "Shared vectors for the Pro features in use notice: a network without Pro whose hosted proxies hold SOCKS or WireGuard (pro.yml puts both in Pro). sdk/pro_features_status_test.go (Go) and js/test/pro_features.test.ts (TypeScript) replay every vector here, so the two implementations cannot drift. status: result is the GET /network/proxies answer as the server sends it (plan: the network holds Pro now, read live, and whether enforce_features is on; each proxy's pro_features: the Pro-only features it holds credentials for), null for no answer, and want is ProFeaturesStatus. A server before the plan sends none, and has no prompt. tracker: each step is update (with the status's prompt), dismiss (the user closed the main screen's notice) or reset (sign out), with the action the tracker returns (post: show and alert; update: show or replace without alerting; remove: withdraw; empty: leave it) and the prompt it shows after the step (empty: none). Client ids are synthetic.",
  "status": [
    {
      "name": "free, enforcement off, a proxy holding SOCKS: the upgrade",
      "result": {
        "clients": [
          { "client_id": "0194b1c0-0000-7000-8000-000000000001", "pro_features": ["socks_proxy"] }
        ],
        "plan": { "pro": false, "pro_features_enforced": false }
      },
      "want": { "prompt": "upgrade", "socks_proxy_count": 1, "wireguard_proxy_count": 0, "plan_known": true, "pro": false, "pro_features_enforced": false }
    },
